# Personal identifiers the export leak-check scans for.
# One extended-regex pattern per line. Blank lines and #-comments are ignored.
#
# WHY THIS FILE MATTERS: without it, export.sh falls back to two built-in generic
# checks (any email address, any Google calendar id) and nothing else. Those catch
# the obvious cases and none of the ones specific to you. Fill this in before you
# publish anything.
#
# This file is never exported -- your identifiers do not belong in a shared repo.
#
# Add, at minimum:
#   - your name, in the spellings that actually occur (given, family, handle)
#   - your email addresses
#   - workspace / account / calendar / list ids from integrations/
#   - employer, client and project names you are under any obligation about
#   - names of family, partners and friends
#
# Examples -- replace these, they match nothing useful as written:
# [Jj]ane
# [Dd]oe
# jane\.doe@
# 1234567
# @group\.calendar\.google\.com
